    "fibre": {
      "scope": "brand",
      "const": "FIBRE",
      "path": "fibre",
      "type": "fibre",
      "absent": "not_assessed",
      "doc": "Measured from the house's own product pages, styles not colourways, men's only. t styles counted (0 = counted, no men's clothing); w styles stating a composition; n/s/c = % of t whose main fibre is natural / synthetic / cellulosic (ruled 13 Sep: cellulosics a third figure); x = % of t with any elastane on the main fabric line; xh = % at 5%+ (0 = counted, none; absent = not counted); sp one|split; sc/nc category lists; st complete|partial. The natural dial is DERIVED at build: band of n/(n+s+c) when w/t >= 0.5, else not assessed. Never stored. cats (optional): list of {cat, house, t, w, n, s, c, x, xh} per product category, the standard set being tees-polos, shirts, knitwear, sweats, trousers, denim, shorts, tailoring, outerwear, underwear-swim, other; when present, t/n/s/c/sp/sc/nc must reconcile to it."
    },
